.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt GREP 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm grep
.Nd search files for lines matching a regular expression (sbase)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl EFHchilnqsvwx
.Op Fl e Ar pattern
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Ar pattern
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is sbase 0.1's
.Nm grep ,
built unpatched for ABSD with the C kit; see
.Xr sbase 7 .
It prints the lines of the named files, or of standard input when none is
named, that match a POSIX basic
.Pq or with Fl E No extended
regular expression, or with
.Fl F
a fixed string.
Unlike
.Xr rg 1 ,
it reads standard input when no file is named, so
.Ql cat f | grep pattern
works, and it does not search directories.
.Sh UNSUPPORTED ON ABSD
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It regular expressions
Picolibc's
.Fn regcomp
and
.Fn regexec ;
C locale only (R14), so
.Fl i
and character classes are ASCII.
.It messages
prefixed with
.Ql argv[0]
as invoked;
.Ql strerror
texts are Picolibc's.
.El
.Pp
Nothing else is refused.
Behaviour on ABSD is predicted until the guest qualification
.Pq Xr sbase 7 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when a line matched, 1 when none did, 2 on an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
absd$ grep -n session /var/log/sshd
absd$ cat /etc/network.conf | grep -c address
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ed 1 ,
.Xr rg 1 ,
.Xr sed 1 ,
.Xr sbase 7
